<task id="defining_the_open_in_excel_button_c7b2e4" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Defining the Open in Excel Button</title>
   <shortdesc>Continue to follow the instructions on the Ribbon Workbench help page to create your button</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Rakesh Singh</author>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>button</keyword>
        <keyword>placeholder</keyword>
        <keyword>click</keyword>
        <keyword>Excel</keyword>
        <keyword>Ribbon</keyword>
        <keyword>Workbench</keyword>
        <indexterm>button</indexterm>
        <indexterm>placeholder</indexterm>
        <indexterm>click</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <context>
         <p>Continue to follow the instructions on the Ribbon Workbench help page to <b>create your button</b> and define your <b>button command</b>.</p>
         <p>Where should I put the Edit in Excel button</p>
         <p>You create the button by clicking on it in the Toolbox and dragging it to <b>Form</b> tab in the Ribbon Workbench.</p>
         <fig>
            <title>98668029</title>
            <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668029.png" width="922" height="557" placement="break">
               <alt>placeholder</alt>
            </image>
         </fig>
         <p>After the button is created, make sure to specify a <b>Label</b> and a 16x16 and 32x32 image. The button Label also automatically defines the button <b>Command </b>name.</p>
         <fig>
            <title>98668030</title>
            <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668030.png" width="832" height="357" placement="break">
               <alt>placeholder</alt>
            </image>
         </fig>
         <p>Because the button uses a JavaScript action to invoke Excel, you will need to specify the following in the Command Properties.</p>
      </context>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the Solutions page, click on the <b>Ribbon Workbench</b>.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668031</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668031.png" width="792" height="396" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the Load Solution pop-up, select the unmanaged solution you created for the button and click <b>OK</b>. This may take several moments to load.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668032</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668032.png" width="426" height="380" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the Solution Elements pane of the Command Bar, click on the Entity picklist and select the entity where you created the button.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668033</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668033.png" width="563" height="388" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Expand the commands section and click on the command you defined for the button.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668034</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668034.png" width="561" height="389" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the Command Properties pane, click <b>Add Action</b> and choose <b>Javascript Action</b> from the picklist.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668035</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668035.png" width="208" height="76" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Click the  icon to find the Web Resource you created that represents the JavaScript code in the solution.</cmd>
            <info>
               <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668036.png" width="21" height="23" placement="inline">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               
            </info>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668037</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668037.png" width="832" height="222" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Finally, you need to add the <b>Function Name</b> from the script to the action. Enter "OpenInExcel" as the function name.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>98668038</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/98667729/98668038.png" width="812" height="220" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>From the top of the Ribbon Workbench, click <b>Publish</b>.

The button is now ready to use from any record for the defined entity.</cmd>
         </step>
      </steps>
   </taskbody>
</task>